<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><IMG SRC="image_001.jpg" ALT="A picture containing text&#10;&#10;Description automatically generated" STYLE="height: 71px; width: 237px"></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><B>Avalon GloboCare Announces 1-for-15 Reverse Stock
Split as Part of Nasdaq Compliance Plan</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><I>&nbsp;</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white"><B>FREEHOLD, N.J., October
24, 2024 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) &ndash; Avalon GloboCare Corp. (&ldquo;Avalon&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;) (NASDAQ: ALBT)</B>, a developer
of innovative precision diagnostics and laboratory services, today announced that it will effect a 1-for-15 reverse split (&ldquo;reverse
split&rdquo;) of its common shares that will become effective on October 28, 2024. The Company expects that the reverse stock split will
allow the Company to regain compliance with the $1.00 minimum bid price requirement of the Nasdaq Capital Market.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white">Avalon GloboCare&rsquo;s
common shares will continue to trade on Nasdaq under the symbol &ldquo;ALBT&rdquo; and will begin trading on a split-adjusted basis when
the market opens on October 28, 2024. The new CUSIP number for the common shares following the reverse split will be 05344R302. The reverse
split will reduce the number of outstanding shares of the Company&rsquo;s common shares from approximately 16.0 million shares to approximately
1.1 million shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&ldquo;This reverse stock
split is a strategic step towards regaining compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s listing requirements,&rdquo; stated David Jin, M.D., Ph.D.,
President and Chief Executive Officer of Avalon GloboCare. &ldquo;It will allow us to continue to execute on our business goals and position
Avalon GloboCare for long-term growth and success. We remain committed to delivering value to our shareholders through our innovative
precision diagnostics and laboratory services.&quot;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><B>About Avalon GloboCare Corp.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><BR>
Avalon GloboCare Corp. (NASDAQ: ALBT) is a commercial stage company dedicated to developing and delivering innovative, transformative,
precision diagnostics and clinical laboratory services. Avalon is working to establish a leading role in the innovation of diagnostic
testing, utilizing proprietary technology to deliver precise, genetics-driven results. The Company also provides laboratory services,
offering a broad portfolio of diagnostic tests, including drug testing, toxicology, and a broad array of test services, from general bloodwork
to anatomic pathology, and urine toxicology. For more information about Avalon GloboCare, please visit www.avalon-globocare.com.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify">For the latest updates on Avalon GloboCare&rsquo;s
developments, please follow our twitter at @avalongc_avco</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

